      "side": 1,
      "message": "optional: Since `second_pred` is always packed with stride `BlockWidth` (`kRowsPerVec` rows are contiguous in memory, as in `SumOfAbsoluteDiff` at line 92), loading `second_pred` directly with `hn::LoadU(pixel_tag, \u0026second_pred[x])` instead of routing it through `LoadRowsU\u003ckRowsPerVec\u003e` avoids 4 separate 128-bit loads + 3 `InsertBlock`s per iteration for `BlockWidth \u003d\u003d 16` (and 2 loads + `ConcatLowerLower` for `BlockWidth \u003d\u003d 32`), which may also eliminate the small-block regression on `16x4` / `16x8` / `16x16`:\n\n```cpp\n      auto src \u003d LoadRowsU\u003ckRowsPerVec\u003e(pixel_tag, \u0026src_ptr[x], src_stride);\n      auto ref \u003d LoadRowsU\u003ckRowsPerVec\u003e(pixel_tag, \u0026ref_ptr[x], ref_stride);\n      auto sec \u003d hn::LoadU(pixel_tag, \u0026second_pred[x]);\n      auto m \u003d LoadRowsU\u003ckRowsPerVec\u003e(pixel_tag, \u0026msk_ptr[x], msk_stride);\n      auto m_inv \u003d hn::Sub(mask_max, m);\n      auto a \u003d invert_mask ? sec : ref;\n      auto b \u003d invert_mask ? ref : sec;\n```",
